    "title": "The Bears have a chance to Showcase their Growth Against Clemson - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Ashmere Prasad ,\n1 days ago Through the first three weeks, the California Bears sit at 2-1, 1-0 in the ACC (4th). The last time the Golden Bears faced the Clemson Tigers, it was a historic matchup. In 1992, the Bears defeated the Tigers 37-13 in the Florida Citrus Bowl. It was the only New Year’s Day bowl game for the Bears since 1959. (calbears.com) Cal is one of three ACC teams to have a winning record against Clemson. But these are two completely different teams from 34 years ago. Read full article",
